UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54001582123425
DTSTART:20261015T210000Z
DTEND:20261015T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Thom Reilly\, professor and co-director of the Center for an Independent and Sustainable Democracy at Arizona State University\, will be speaking at FSU about his soon to be published book: "Child Abduction in the War in Ukraine: Erasing Ukrainian Identity as a Tool of War" (2027)\n\nThe lecture\, "Erasing Ukrainian Identity: The Abdusction of Ukrainian Children as a Tool of War\," is sponsored by the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy's Ruth K. and Shepard Broad International Lecture Series and the Center for Global Engagement's Engage Your World Speaker Series. \n\nThe event\, which is free and open to the public\, will take place at 5:30 p.m. Thursday\, October 15th\, at The Globe Auditorium\, 110 S. Woodward Ave. A pre-lecture reception will take place at 5 p.m.
GEO:30.440771;-84.298448
LOCATION:Global and Multicultural Engagement Building (GME)\, Auditorium
SUMMARY:Erasing Ukrainian Identity: The Abduction of Ukrainian Children as a Tool of War
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/erasing-ukrainian-identity-the-abduction-of-ukrainian-children-as-a-tool-of-war
END:VEVENT
